                <section id="expert-guidance" className="scroll-mt-32">
                  <h3 className="text-lg md:text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-3 mt-6">Why Expert Guidance Matters in Financial Crises</h3>
                  <p className="text-sm md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4 text-gray-700">
                    Attempting to resolve a massive debt burden independently is akin to navigating a minefield blindfolded. Banks and Non-Banking Financial Companies employ highly trained recovery units and legal teams whose sole objective is to maximize the extraction of funds from the borrower. They utilize complex mathematical models to calculate compound interest, penal charges, and late fees, creating a financial labyrinth that is intentionally difficult for the average consumer to decipher. This is why expert guidance is not just a luxury; it is an absolute necessity.
                  </p>
                  <p className="text-sm md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4 text-gray-700">
                    An expert debt counsellor brings a wealth of specialized knowledge to the table. They understand the internal policies of different banking institutions, they know the legal limitations of recovery agents, and they are intimately familiar with the Reserve Bank of India guidelines governing fair practices. When a borrower attempts to negotiate a loan settlement on their own, they often make critical errors. They might inadvertently admit to liabilities they do not owe, or they might agree to verbal settlements that the bank later denies, leading to further financial ruin.
                  </p>
                  <p className="text-sm md:text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4 text-gray-700">
                    Furthermore, the psychological support provided by a reputable counsellor cannot be overstated. The stress of constant harassment can lead to severe anxiety and depression, severely impairing a person's ability to make rational decisions. A professional advisor absorbs this pressure, handling all communications with the lenders and providing the borrower with the mental space required to rebuild their life. They systematically analyze your income, essential expenses, and total liabilities to craft a realistic roadmap out of debt.
                  </p>
                </section>

                {/* 2. Key Indicators */}
